  "name": null,
  "problem": "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{148}$ be a random sample of size $n=148$ from a population with a population mean $\\mu =98$ and population standard deviation $\\sigma =74.$ Find an approximation for the probability that the sample mean is greater than $95.$\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.2843\\,$ | $\\,0.2810\\,$ | $\\,0.2776\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3192\\,$ | $\\,0.3156\\,$ | $\\,0.3121\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ | $\\,0.3520\\,$ | $\\,0.3483\\,$ |",
